What this computer trusts for TUR's updates (ADR-0023;
docs/architecture/publishing.md in the TUR repository).

The container policy, /usr/share/containers/policy.json, accepts an image
named ghcr.io/giorgiogiudice/tur only with a sigstore signature that verifies
with release.pub and is recorded in Sigstore's public transparency log, whose
key is rekor.pub. Images from anywhere else are not affected.

release.pub   TUR's release key, the public half (ECDSA P-256), made by the
              project's owner. Its private half is held by the release
              workflow on GitHub and by the owner offline, nowhere else.
rekor.pub     The public key of Sigstore's Rekor transparency log at
              https://rekor.sigstore.dev, as Sigstore's signed trust root
              names it. The policy uses it to check offline that a signature
              was entered in the public log.
fulcio.crt    The certificate chain of Sigstore's Fulcio certificate
              authority at https://fulcio.sigstore.dev. Each published image
              also carries a keyless signature made with the release
              workflow's own identity; this chain verifies it. The container
              libraries in this image cannot yet match a workflow identity
              (they match an e-mail address only), so the policy does not
              use it.

rekor.pub and fulcio.crt are Sigstore's public trust data, copied unchanged
from Sigstore's trust root (scripts/release/trust-roots.py); they are not
under the TUR licence.
